# ==============================================================================
# KRITOMATIC ENVIRONMENT CONFIGURATION
# ==============================================================================
# INSTALLATION:
# This file MUST be placed at: ~/.config/xremap/xremap_kritomatic.env
#
# PURPOSE:
# This file provides the local paths and device settings for the
# xremap-kritomatic systemd service.
# ==============================================================================

# 1. REPOSITORY PATH
# The absolute path to the directory where this repository is cloned.
REPODIR="/path/to/your/cloned/repo"

# 2. PERSONAL CONFIGURATION (OPTIONAL)
# Path to an additional personal xremap configuration file.
# LEAVE EMPTY ("") if you do not have a secondary config file.
PERSONAL_CONFIG=""

# 3. TARGET DEVICE (OPTIONAL)
# The hardware device name to target (e.g., "kanata ministeren").
# Run 'xremap --list-devices' to see available names.
# LEAVE EMPTY ("") to apply shortcuts to ALL connected input devices.
TARGET_DEVICE=""

# 4. ADDITIONAL DEVICES (OPTIONAL)
# Comma-separated list of extra device names that xremap should ALSO listen on,
# in addition to TARGET_DEVICE. Useful when your main keyboard is a different
# device than the peripheral TARGET_DEVICE (e.g. kanata emits your main
# keyboard as "kanata standard" while a macropad is "kanata ministeren").
#
# Bindings in TARGET_DEVICE's config still only fire from TARGET_DEVICE unless
# the individual binding has an explicit "device:" block in its source YAML
# (e.g. the C-v entry in PERSONAL_CONFIG can opt into "kanata standard" here).
#
# LEAVE EMPTY ("") if you only want xremap to listen on TARGET_DEVICE.
# Example: PERSONAL_DEVICES="kanata standard"
PERSONAL_DEVICES=""
